# Work queue

See [handlers](/docs/applications/handlers/) for the role table. This example
is the programming-model sibling of the [handler matrix](/examples/handler-matrix/).
The matrix lists every accepted verb. This queue shows which role to reach for
in a real app.

SQLite owns the jobs. Components stay pure. Datastar carries intent and morphs
HTML. Generated dispatch uses **literal** paths: row ids travel in the JSON
body, not `/actions/claim/${id}`.

| Interaction | Route | Morph |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Document | `@get:view("/")` | Full page |
| Reset composer | `@get:fragment("/fragments/composer")` | `#composer` in this tab |
| Validate title | `@post:fragment("/actions/validate")` | `#composer` in this tab |
| Inspect a job | `@post:fragment("/actions/inspect")` | `#inspect` in this tab |
| Enqueue | `@post:command("/actions/enqueue")` | None |
| Claim | `@post:command("/actions/claim")` | None |
| Complete | `@delete:command("/actions/complete")` | None |
| Shared board | `@get:live("/sse")` | `#queue` and `#activity` in every tab |

Do not morph `#queue` from a fragment. Do not morph `#inspect` from live.

This catalog row is **docs-only**. Do not expose it as a public origin; use
local `curl` against `rocci run`. Source files are listed in the sidebar.

## Run locally

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- run examples/rocci/standalone/work-queue/WorkQueue.rocci
```

Open the printed URL in two windows. Inspect in one; the other inspect well
stays waiting and both logs update. Enqueue or claim; only the shared board
moves.

## Smoke

```sh
curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8000/health
curl -s -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/actions/inspect \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  --data '{"job_id":"1"}'
curl -s -D - -o /dev/null -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/actions/enqueue \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  --data '{"title":"From curl"}'
```
